  "content": {
    "id": "p7-q6-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "Consider the function\n$$f(x)=\\begin{cases}-x,&x<0,\\\\4-2x,&x\\ge0.\\end{cases}$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p7-q6-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Sketch the graph of $y=f(x)$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y=-x$ for $x<0$, with an open endpoint at $(0,0)$; $y=4-2x$ for $x\\ge0$, with a closed endpoint at $(0,4)$.",
          "worked": "For $x<0$, draw the part of $y=-x$ to the left of the $y$-axis, excluding $(0,0)$. For $x\\ge0$, draw the part of $y=4-2x$ on and to the right of the $y$-axis, including $(0,4)$ and passing through $(2,0)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": [
            {
              "id": "p7-q6-a-solution-graph",
              "role": "solution",
              "format": "tikz",
              "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"graph\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[],\"reference\":\"source page 7 question 6(a); teacher page 32\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.55cm,y=0.38cm]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\path[use as bounding box] (-5.1,-5.8) rectangle (5.5,5.5);\n\\draw[->,line width=0.5pt] (-5,0)--(5,0) node[right] {$x$};\n\\draw[->,line width=0.5pt] (0,-5.2)--(0,5.1) node[above] {$y$};\n\\draw[black,line width=0.8pt] plot[domain=-5:0,samples=2] (\\x,{-\\x});\n\\draw[black,line width=0.8pt] plot[domain=0:4.5,samples=2] (\\x,{4-2*\\x});\n\\filldraw[draw=black,fill=white,line width=0.8pt] (0,0) circle[radius=2pt];\n\\fill[black] (0,4) circle[radius=2pt];\n\\node[below left] at (0,0) {$(0,0)$};\n\\node[right] at (0,4) {$(0,4)$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
              "src": null,
              "widthMm": 60,
              "alt": "Mathematical diagram",
              "overlayOf": null,
              "transparent": false,
              "axes": null,
              "spec": {
                "sourcePage": 7,
                "sourceRegion": "Question 6(a); teacher PDF page 32, Section B, question 6(a)",
                "description": "Two linear branches with an open point at the origin and a closed point at (0,4). Axes have arrows and no ticks or grid, as in the teacher sketch. Ordinary source-blue curves are rendered black under house style.",
                "mathematics": "y=-x for x<0; y=4-2x for x>=0. The right branch crosses the x-axis at x=2.",
                "answerVisibility": "Solution only; the student question supplies neither axes nor a graph."
              },
              "derived": false,
              "reviewStatus": "needs-review"
            }
          ]
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 65
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-q6-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the value(s) of $a$ for which $f(a)=3$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$a=-3$ or $a=\\frac12$.",
          "worked": "For $a<0$:\n$$\\begin{align*}-a&=3\\\\a&=-3.\\end{align*}$$\nThis satisfies $a<0$.\n\nFor $a\\ge0$:\n$$\\begin{align*}4-2a&=3\\\\2a&=1\\\\a&=\\frac12.\\end{align*}$$\nThis satisfies $a\\ge0$. Hence $a=-3$ or $a=\\frac12$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-q6-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Find the value(s) of $a$ for which $f(-a)=f(a)$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$a=-\\frac43,\\ 0,\\ \\frac43$.\n\nUse opposite branches when $a\\ne0$ and check $a=0$ separately.",
          "worked": "For $a>0$, $-a<0$, so $f(-a)=a$ and $f(a)=4-2a$:\n$$\\begin{align*}a&=4-2a\\\\3a&=4\\\\a&=\\frac43.\\end{align*}$$\nThis satisfies $a>0$.\n\nFor $a<0$, $-a>0$, so $f(-a)=4+2a$ and $f(a)=-a$:\n$$\\begin{align*}4+2a&=-a\\\\3a&=-4\\\\a&=-\\frac43.\\end{align*}$$\nThis satisfies $a<0$.\n\nFor $a=0$, $f(-0)=f(0)=4$, so $a=0$ also satisfies the equation.\n\nHence $a=-\\frac43,\\ 0,\\ \\frac43$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      }
    ]
  },
